<!-- <STRONG>PILOT SCALE AEROSOL MANUFACTURING</STRONG> -->
<section class="section" id="pilot-scale-aerosol-manufacturing">
  <h2><strong>Pilot Scale Aerosol Manufacturing</strong></h2>
  <p>Pilot scale is the bridge between laboratory success and commercial feasibility. At this stage, the
            formulation is produced using semi-industrial equipment to validate heat transfer, mixing energy, propellant
            dissolution, pressure behavior, and filling parameters. Pilot trials also reveal real-world issues that are
            not visible during laboratory work, such as foaming during filling or delayed phase separation.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Validation of concentrate mixing at higher volumes</li>
            <li>Testing propellant loading through pilot gassing lines</li>
            <li>Valve, actuator, stem-bore, and orifice-size compatibility assessment</li>
            <li>Short-term and accelerated storage behavior evaluation</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><strong>Typical Batch Sizes</strong></h3>
        <ul>
            <li>20–200 kg bulk concentrate</li>
            <li>500–5,000 filled aerosol cans</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><strong>Pilot Equipment</strong></h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Jacketed SS mixing vessels</li>
            <li>Pilot-scale homogenizers</li>
            <li>Semi-automatic crimpers</li>
            <li>Single-head or double-head gassing machines</li>
        </ul>

