<!-- <STRONG>FAQS</STRONG> -->
<section class="section" id="faqs">
  <h2><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>
  <h3>Can aerosol production start without pilot trials?</h3>
        <p>No. Aerosol products must undergo pilot validation to check propellant stability, valve performance, filling
            behavior, and spray characteristics. Skipping this step leads to high failure rates during commercial
            manufacturing.</p>

        <h3>How long does it take to go from R&D to commercial launch?</h3>
        <p>Depending on the product category, the timeline ranges from 3 months for simple aerosols to 18 months for
            high-performance or industrial aerosols requiring extended testing.</p>

        <h3>Do formulations change during scale-up?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Most aerosol products undergo controlled adjustments in propellant ratios, solvent balance, inhibitor
            levels, or valve selection to optimize performance at commercial scale.</p>
</section>

